# Note 05 — Building the Study Area and First Dataset
Date: 2026-11-15

## Pipeline
Official PDF map → georeference → trace boundary → 500 m grid → upload to GEE
→ Landsat processing (clouds, scaling, indices) → zonal statistics per cell → CSV (1 row per cell)

## Key choices and reasons
| Step | Choice | Why | Alternative rejected |
|---|---|---|---|
| Boundary source | MCG map (28 Dec 2020), georeferenced | Official boundary; only available as image | Trace by eye (inaccurate); paid data (licence) |
| Control points | 8, spread across the map | Polynomial 1 needs ≥3; extra points measure and average error | Clustered points → edges drift |
| Transformation | Polynomial 1 | Shift, scale, rotate; keeps straight lines straight | Polynomial 2/3, thin plate spline → bend/hide errors |
| Quality check | Residuals 0.27–1.07 px | Small and similar → points agree | — |
| CRS | EPSG:32643 (UTM 43N) | Metres; Gurugram (77°E) in zone 72–78°E | Degrees (EPSG:4326) cannot give 500 m cells |
| Unit | 500 m grid, 1,033 cells | No public ward map; avoids zoning effect; ~25 thermal pixels per cell | 100 m (noisy, ≈ thermal pixel); 1 km (hides neighbourhoods) |
| File format | GeoPackage; Shapefile only for GEE upload | One file, no field-name limits | — |
| Season | Mar–May 2025 | Peak heat, before monsoon clouds | Monsoon (clouds); winter (weak contrast) |
| Cloud filtering | Scene CLOUD_COVER < 10 + QA_PIXEL bits 1–4 | Two sieves: whole scene, then pixel | — |
| Composite | Median | Robust to leftover clouds/outliers | Mean (pulled by outliers) |
| Zonal stats | reduceRegions, mean, scale 30 | Average every 30 m pixel inside each cell | — |

## Reference numbers
- Landsat 8/9 bands: B4 red · B5 NIR · B6 SWIR1 · B10 thermal
- QA_PIXEL bits: 1 dilated cloud · 2 cirrus · 3 cloud · 4 cloud shadow
- 1,033 cells × 0.25 km² ≈ 258 km² upper bound (edge cells are partial)

